! **Ten sites.** Diamond silicon, five primitive cells stacked along `a3` --
! 10 atoms, which is the size at which a comparison against QE stops measuring
! fixed overheads and starts measuring the physics, and which no committed case
! here reached (the largest were the 8-atom cubic cells).
!
! The cell is `(a1, a2, 5 a3)` on the standard fcc primitive vectors, so it is a
! **supercell** in QE's sense -- `is_supercell` fires, fractional translations
! are discarded, and what is left is the 6-operation C_3v the [111] axis
! survives with. That group is the whole reason this case exists: the images of
! `a3` under those rotations need coefficients of **five** in the supercell
! basis (`s(2) = ((0,-1,0),(1,-1,0),(0,-5,1))` as `pw.x -v high` prints it), and
! the lattice point group was searched over a hardcoded `range(-3, 4)` window,
! which found 2 operations where QE finds 6. Both codes converge; the two
! densities are symmetrised over different groups and the total energies part
! company at **3.2e-6 Ry**. With the window replaced by the exact metric bound
! (`|n_j| <= max_i |a_i| |b_j|`) they agree to **3e-9 Ry**, and the SCF is
! twice as fast because it symmetrises over six operations instead of two.
!
! `ecutwfc` and the pseudopotential are `pw_scf/scf.in`'s, so what this case
! adds over that one is the cell and nothing else. The 4x4x1 grid is the
! primitive 4x4x5 folded: `A3` is five times longer, so its reciprocal vector is
! a fifth as long.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, celldm(1) = 10.20, nat = 10, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 12.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  -0.50  0.00  0.50
   0.00  0.50  0.50
  -2.50  2.50  0.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000
 Si    0.2500    0.2500    0.2500
 Si   -0.5000    0.5000    0.0000
 Si   -0.2500    0.7500    0.2500
 Si   -1.0000    1.0000    0.0000
 Si   -0.7500    1.2500    0.2500
 Si   -1.5000    1.5000    0.0000
 Si   -1.2500    1.7500    0.2500
 Si   -2.0000    2.0000    0.0000
 Si   -1.7500    2.2500    0.2500
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 1 0 0 0
